.TH touch 1 "FUZIX System Utilities" "FUZIX"
.SH NAME
touch \- update file timestamps, or create empty files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B touch
[\fB\-c\fR] \fIfile ...\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
For each
.I file
that exists,
.B touch
sets both the access and the modification time to now.  For each one
that does not, it creates an empty file with mode 0666 less the
.BR umask .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-c
Do not create missing files; pass over them quietly.
.PP
.B \-c
is only recognised as the
.I first
argument.
.SH NOTES
There is no way to set a time other than the present: no
.BR \-t ,
no
.BR \-r ,
no
.BR \-d .
.PP
Running
.B touch
with no arguments at all reads past the end of the argument list.  Give
it at least one name.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR date (1),
.BR ls (1)
